    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Drake Baldwin** (69.51) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) serving as our primary offensive anchors. Both players benefit significantly from the favorable matchup against Randy Dobnak and Brady Singer, respectively, with **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s top-of-the-order role and **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s advantageous platoon positioning pushing them well into the \"Strong\" start tier. **Henry Bolte** also warrants attention as a high-upside play (59.84); while he faces a decent arm in Peter Lambert, his projected leadoff spot and a 10% park factor bump make him an essential engine for our runs and stolen base potential. Given the scarcity of SB in this league, **Henry Bolte**\u2019s speed remains a primary driver for his selection over lower-ceiling options.\n\nWhile the lineup is largely optimized, **Andy Pages** (44.47) stands as the most difficult omission. His base projection remained competitive, but he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer volume of better matchups for players like **Luis Lara** and **Heliot Ramos**. We are closely monitoring the status of **Liam Hicks**, **Tommy White**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Henry Bolte**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**; because their spots are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" any drastic shifts in their projected batting order could compress their efficiency scores. Additionally, we must exercise caution with **Jackson Merrill** and **Kyle Tucker**, as both draw tough matchups against high-end arms like Tyler Glasnow and Nick Pivetta, respectively. Despite the elite talent, their scores are suppressed by these pitching matchups, requiring us to prioritize the daily efficiency of players like **Miguel Vargas** (58.95), who remains a solid utility play due to his favorable park and strong xwOBA profile.",
